// extdeps/hardware.dag — the electronic-hardware domain marker.
//
// "Hardware" here is electronic hardware: the physical devices/components a system
// is built from (CPUs, GPUs, DRAM, …) — the real-world domain that the per-vendor
// catalogs under extdeps/{cpu,memory}/ and product/compute_fabric model. It is a
// domain TAG, not a universal framework, so it lives downstream of std (extdeps),
// not in std. It is the type argument that specializes the generic Vendor concept:
// a hardware maker is a `Vendor<Hardware>` (extdeps/vendor.dag).
// Anchor: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electronic_hardware

module extdeps.hardware

// Phantom domain marker (no inhabitants of its own — same deferral shape as
// std.ReferenceModel<T> / the Measure phantom scales). It exists only to specialize
// `Vendor<Domain>`; a richer hardware taxonomy decomposes here when a consumer needs
// to dispatch on it (DESIGN §6 model just-in-time).
type Hardware
